    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "If we take Word2Vec apart, which idea truly changed the direction of research?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Before word2vec, many NLP systems relied on sparse counts or hand-built features. Word2vec made dense vectors practical at web scale.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-efficient-estimation-of-word-representations-in-vector-space"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "The model predicts context from a word or a word from context, forcing related words to occupy nearby regions of vector space. The key mechanism is Skip-gram and CBOW neural word embeddings, which links the source material to the visible demo behavior.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-efficient-estimation-of-word-representations-in-vector-space"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Experts generally treat Word2Vec as a foundational embedding method that made distributional semantics operational at scale. Its long-term legacy is the geometric view of meaning that still informs retrieval, representation learning, and vector databases.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-efficient-estimation-of-word-representations-in-vector-space"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Seen alongside Neural Language Model, Word2Vec reveals how the same technical question can echo across different eras.",
